# Core function shape

Applies when adding or changing functions under `pkgs/core/src/`.

## Layout

- One directory per function: `pkgs/core/src/<camelCaseName>/`.
- Implement in `index.ts` with a **named export** matching the directory name.
- Co-locate unit tests in `test.ts`.
- Do not use directory names that collide with reserved areas (`locale`, `fp`, `constants`, `tp`, or `_`-prefixed / dotted names used by tooling).

## Documentation

Use TSDoc on the public export, including at least:

- `@name`, `@category`, `@summary`, `@description`, `@example`

Pick `@category` from the list in `pkgs/core/docs/config.js` (e.g. Day Helpers, Common Helpers).

## Generated surfaces

Build scripts regenerate package exports, root indexes, and FP wrappers. Do not hand-edit generated FP files or casually rewrite package export maps—follow existing build/contribution flow.

When touching FP behavior, see `pkgs/core/docs/fp.md` (curried functions, reversed argument order, `WithOptions` variants).
